2026-11-07T11:51:14.2230675Z [34m---- let's talk about sudo -----------------------------------------------------
2026-11-07T11:51:14.2240573Z [0mThis script is going to call sudo a lot. Normally, it would show you
2026-11-07T11:51:14.2241368Z exactly what commands it is running and why. However, the script is
2026-11-07T11:51:14.2241843Z run in a headless fashion, like this:
2026-11-07T11:51:14.2242160Z 
2026-11-07T11:51:14.2242441Z   $ curl -L https://nixos.org/nix/install | sh
2026-11-07T11:51:14.2242691Z 
2026-11-07T11:51:14.2242947Z or maybe in a CI pipeline. Because of that, I'm going to skip the
2026-11-07T11:51:14.2243420Z verbose output in the interest of brevity.
2026-11-07T11:51:14.2243702Z 
2026-11-07T11:51:14.2243867Z If you would like to
2026-11-07T11:51:14.2244485Z see the output, try like this:
2026-11-07T11:51:14.2244697Z 
2026-11-07T11:51:14.2245487Z   $ curl -L -o install-nix https://nixos.org/nix/install
2026-11-07T11:51:14.2245980Z   $ sh ./install-nix
2026-11-07T11:51:14.2246163Z 
